%%begintext 
These are basically reels, but they reflect the dance culture of the central/southern
US, where they're often called hoedowns. are popular contest pieces, usually elaborated in
the "controlled improvisation" style pioneered by Eck Robertson, Benny Thomasson, Byron Berline,
and others.
